# <%= module %>

An independent Nerves Gate SDK application. From the workspace root:

```sh
mix app.install <%= app %>
mix app.package <%= app %>
```

Run ordinary host unit tests in this directory with `mix test`, or test all apps
with `mix test` at the workspace root. Device services come from the real firmware
inside QEMU or on a physical gateway; there is no fake hardware backend.

`mix nerves_gate.package` also works directly in this directory. It builds a
standard OTP `.ez` archive containing the app and private runtime dependencies,
not the SDK or platform libraries. Code and `NervesGateSDK.Storage.data_dir(:<%= app %>)`
live on the commissioned SD card. Handle unavailable storage explicitly.

Packages run trusted code in the firmware BEAM, not a sandbox. Native code must
be built for the device architecture. Upgrades are cold restarts with a bounded
`health_check/0`, not OTP hot-code upgrades.
